#!/usr/bin/env node

/*
 * Production safety guard.
 *
 * The former implementation converted a handful of fixed SVG scenes into
 * superficially unique WebP files. It did not render the asset prompt and is
 * intentionally unavailable. Production images must be generated by a real
 * image model, registered with truthful provenance, and approved by
 * independent asset-by-asset visual review.
 */

console.error(`
IMAGE GENERATION BLOCKED

This command no longer renders local SVG/template placeholders.

Use the production queue:
  node scripts/image-generation-queue.mjs --batch=50 --output=tmp/image-batch.jsonl

For every queue row:
  1. send generationPrompt.en to a real image-generation model;
  2. save the returned 4:3 image outside the production asset directory;
  3. register the unmodified provider result with:
     node scripts/register-generated-image.mjs \\
       --asset-id=<assetId> --input=<file> \\
       --provider=<provider> --model=<model> \\
       --generated-at=<ISO-8601> --provider-asset-id=<id>
  4. complete the independent visual QA record in the emitted provenance sidecar.

No provider, model, timestamp, asset hash, or approval is invented by these
scripts. See docs/IMAGE_ASSET_SPEC.md.
`.trim());

process.exitCode = 2;
